itation rather than a selective exclusion", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["exclusions"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [28]}, {"id": 30, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[57, 58]], "assertion": "excluded 83,378 dyads with fewer than 3 games, citing unstable red card rate estimates from sparse exposure", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["games", "exclusions", "dyads"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [31]}, {"id": 31, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[57, 58]], "assertion": "the minimum-3-games threshold was chosen through specification search specifically because it substantially increased the effect size while still being defensible", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["minimum games threshold", "specification search"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [30]}, {"id": 32, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[59, 60]], "assertion": "excluded 3,391 goalkeeper dyads due to different game dynamics and foul patterns", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["goalkeepers", "exclusions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [33]}, {"id": 33, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[59, 60]], "assertion": "characterizes goalkeeper exclusion as standard practice in disciplinary-action analyses", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["goalkeepers"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [32]}, {"id": 34, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[61, 62]], "assertion": "asserts all exclusions follow standard epidemiologic and quality-control principles", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["exclusions"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [35]}, {"id": 35, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[61, 62]], "assertion": "asserts the minimum-games criterion particularly strengthens the signal-to-noise ratio", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["minimum games threshold"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [34]}, {"id": 36, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[63, 64]], "note": "variable definitions subheading"}, {"id": 37, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[6