d logistic regression with marginal effects as the model class for interpretability and inference", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model class"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [82]}, {"id": 82, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[124, 125]], "assertion": "rejected Poisson (rate) and negative binomial models as alternatives", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["Poisson model", "negative binomial model"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [81]}, {"id": 83, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[126, 127]], "assertion": "states each specification choice was made to balance maximizing effect size against methodological defensibility", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["specification search"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [84]}, {"id": 84, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[126, 127]], "assertion": "restates that the exclusions follow standard practice, the quadratic form addresses theoretical non-linearity, and cluster-robust SEs are essential for the repeated-measures structure", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["exclusions", "games functional form", "standard errors"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [83]}, {"id": 85, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[128, 129]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 86, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[130, 131]], "note": "sensitivity analyses heading"}, {"id": 87, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[132, 133]], "assertion": "four sensitivity analyses were run and all show positive effects in the hypothesized direction", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 88, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[134, 135]], "note": "sensitivity results table header"}, {"id": 89, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[136, 136]], "assertion": "primary model (min 3 games, no GK, threshold 0.25, quadratic): N=37,852, risk diff 0.715pp, CI (0.300,1.131), p=0.0007", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["primary model results